From f8abf84ea16d508cc81851ef22861613dcfc34f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneshot <oneshot@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:01:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] friends: say when the relay refuses the lasting code; typed
 and Direct-only codes work

- The host notes in friends-kept.txt (ok/refused) whether the relay served the
  lasting nameplate, and the game status says so (horizon.friends.kept_refused);
  the Android launcher shows it on the friends page.
- A guest in Direct only still joins a short code through the relay.
- friend: is matched without regard to case.
- A code typed by hand in the launcher is saved as friend:CODE, as Paste does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
